  {
   "id": "lLnBRlF1BQAJ",
   "from": "Vera In Wehen",
   "author": "0f69df8ec3bab1e8",
   "date": "2020-06-04T18:14:27Z",
   "subject": "Re: Script of the model",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Dear Brandon, <div><br></div><div>thank you so, so much! I just started using R and I&#39;m still having a hard time. </div><div>I do have one question. I&#39;m not sure if the script includes it, but the idea of the model is that A+B is the input/independent, C+D the mediators, and E+F dependent/outcome. </div><div><br></div><div>So the hypothesis would be </div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:black;line-height:20px\"></p><ol><li><span style=\"font-size:small\">D mediates the relationship between B and E</span><br></li><li><span style=\"font-size:small\">D mediates the relationship between A and E</span><br></li><li><span style=\"font-size:small\">C mediates the relationship between B and E</span><br></li><li><span style=\"font-size:small\">C mediates the relationship between A and E</span><br></li><li><span style=\"font-size:small\">D mediates the relationship between B and F</span><br></li><li><span style=\"font-size:small\">D mediates the relationship between A and F</span><br></li><li><span style=\"font-size:small\">C mediates the relationship between B and F</span><br></li><li><span style=\"font-size:small\">C mediates the relationship between A and F</span><br></li></ol><div><font size=\"2\">Thank you so much!</font></div><p></p></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "doUn4F52BQAJ",
   "from": "Brandon McCormick",
   "author": "bb2081cebf8f7c8c",
   "date": "2020-06-04T18:33:44Z",
   "subject": "Re: Script of the model",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Yes, that seems correct! You could also estimate the direct paths by adding <div><br></div><div>E ~ A</div><div>E ~ B</div><div>F ~ A</div><div>F ~ B<br><div><br></div><div><br></div></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Thu, Jun 4, 2020 at 1:14 PM Vera In Wehen &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">Milli.R...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Dear Brandon, <div><br></div><div>thank you so, so much! I just started using R and I&#39;m still having a hard time. </div><div>I do have one question. I&#39;m not sure if the script includes it, but the idea of the model is that A+B is the input/independent, C+D the mediators, and E+F dependent/outcome. </div><div><br></div><div>So the hypothesis would be </div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:black;line-height:20px\"></p><ol><li><span style=\"font-size:small\">D mediates the relationship between B and E</span><br></li><li><span style=\"font-size:small\">D mediates the relationship between A and E</span><br></li><li><span style=\"font-size:small\">C mediates the relationship between B and E</span><br></li><li><span style=\"font-size:small\">C mediates the relationship between A and E</span><br></li><li><span style=\"font-size:small\">D mediates the relationship between B and F</span><br></li><li><span style=\"font-size:small\">D mediates the relationship between A and F</span><br></li><li><span style=\"font-size:small\">C mediates the relationship between B and F</span><br></li><li><span style=\"font-size:small\">C mediates the relationship between A and F</span><br></li></ol><div><font size=\"2\">Thank you so much!</font></div><p></p></div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p></blockquote></div>"
